  "instructions": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat.",
    "Add the minced garlic and ginger and cook for 1 minute, until fragrant.",
    "Add the cumin, coriander, paprika, cayenne pepper, salt, and black pepper. Cook for 1 minute, stirring constantly.",
    "Add the shrimp and cook for 2-3 minutes per side, until pink and cooked through.",
    "Transfer the shrimp to a plate and set aside.",
    "In the same skillet, add the bulgur, tomatoes, parsley, and mint leaves. Cook for 2-3 minutes, until the bulgur is lightly toasted.",
    "Stir in the lacquer glaze, water, soy sauce, and honey. Bring the mixture to a simmer and cook for 1-2 minutes, until the glaze has thickened.",
    "Return the shrimp to the skillet and toss to coat with the lacquer glaze.",
    "Serve the shrimp over the tabbouleh and garnish with additional parsley, if desired.",
    "Refrigerate the leftovers for up to 3 days.",
    "Serve in a lacquerware bowl for a traditional touch.",
    "Adjust the seasoning as needed and serve immediately."
